{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WTpxM8XmSfYT5ii1yqfhtf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tI have everything I need: the B6/B7 contracts, the eight published cross-bearings into Ch 10 (four section-pinned), the cached sources, and Ch 9's shipped handoff. One significant collision surfaced — Ch 3 §4 already *named* the absent-component pattern that B6 assigns Ch 10 to name.\n2\t\n3\t---\n4\t\n5\t```\n6\t---\n7\tchapter: 10\n8\tchapter_type: \"content\"\n9\ttitle: \"Traffic from Beyond the Cluster\"\n10\tsubtitle: \"Frozen, superseded, and inert without a controller\"\n11\texam_domain: \"Container Orchestration (competency: Networking)\"\n12\tdomain_weight_pct: 5\n13\tcomplexity: \"mixed\"\n14\tnovelty: \"moderate\"\n15\tprereq_factor: \"heavy\"\n16\t\n17\t#-- SUBTITLE NOTE. The arc outline's working subtitle is \"Ingress is\n18\t#-- frozen, Gateway is the future, and neither does anything without a\n19\t#-- controller\" — fourteen words against this stage's ≤10-word\n20\t#-- constraint. Tightened above to seven. The compression is not just\n21\t#-- length: \"inert\" is the word §7 needs for a NetworkPolicy on an\n22\t#-- unsupporting plugin, and using it in the subtitle makes the\n23\t#-- subtitle cover BOTH halves of the chapter rather than only the\n24\t#-- Ingress half. The arc's version names Ingress and Gateway and stops\n25\t#-- there, which under-describes a chapter that is 40% NetworkPolicy.\n26\t#-- Arc-faithful alternative preserved in § Open questions #1.\n27\t\n28\t#-- EXAM_DOMAIN NOTE. Recorded as D2.1 Networking, matching Ch 9's house\n29\t#-- form. The arc outline scopes this chapter \"D2.1 (+ D2.2 boundary)\"\n30\t#-- because NetworkPolicy is listed under BOTH D2.1 Networking and D2.2\n31\t#-- Security in B1's concept map. B2's ordering rule #6 settles it:\n32\t#-- teach NetworkPolicy once, in Networking, and cross-bear from\n33\t#-- Security. This chapter is where it is taught. Ch 12 §9 refers and\n34\t#-- never redefines. kb_tags carries both objective IDs.\n35\t\n36\t#-- PREREQ NOTE. `heavy`, not `standard` — the first `heavy` in Part III.\n37\t#-- B2 lists exactly one prerequisite chapter for this chapter (Ch 9),\n38\t#-- which looks light until you notice it means ALL of Ch 9. This\n39\t#-- chapter re-teaches no part of the Service model: §1's argument is\n40\t#-- arithmetic on Ch 9 §3's ladder, §2's backends are Ch 9's Services,\n41\t#-- §6's subjects are Ch 4's selectors pointed at Ch 9's Pod IPs. A\n42\t#-- reader who skipped Ch 9 cannot start here. The Soundings rubric's\n43\t#-- 0–2 branch must say so in as many words.\n44\t\n45\t#-- Section plan (no word budgets) ---------------------------------------\n46\t#-- Length is content-driven. Arc-outline depth band: \"standard\" — 5\n47\t#-- points. Planning signal only, NOT a target.\n48\t#--\n49\t#-- ⚠ SECTION NUMBERING IS LOAD-BEARING. Eight published cross-bearings\n50\t#-- point into this chapter and FOUR name a section by number — all four\n51\t#-- from Chapter 9, which shipped 2026-08-24:\n52\t#--   chapter-09 line  544 → *[... see Ch 10 §1 — the exposure ceiling and what crosses it]*\n53\t#--   chapter-09 line 1056 → *[... see Ch 10 §2 — name-based virtual hosting]*\n54\t#--   chapter-09 line  407 → *[... see Ch 10 §6 — NetworkPolicy]*\n55\t#--   chapter-09 line 1706 → *[... see Ch 10 §6 — NetworkPolicy]*\n56\t#-- All four match the B6 skeleton exactly. §1, §2 and §6 below are\n57\t#-- fixed. Do not renumber without editing chapter-09 in four places.\n58\t#-- Verified 2026-08-25 against chapters 01–09.\n59\tsections:\n60\t  - name: \"Where LoadBalancer Runs Out\"\n61\t    objectives: [\"D2.1\"]\n62\t    requires_figure: true\n63\t    figure_anchor: \"ch10-fig01-ingress-vs-service-loadbalancer\"\n64\t    checkpoint_after: false\n65\t  - name: \"Routing by Host and Path\"\n66\t    objectives: [\"D2.1\"]\n67\t    requires_figure: true\n68\t    figure_anchor: \"ch10-fig02-ingress-fanout-and-name-based-hosts\"\n69\t    checkpoint_after: false\n70\t  - name: \"The Object Is Not the Implementation\"\n71\t    objectives: [\"D2.1\"]\n72\t    requires_figure: false\n73\t    figure_anchor: null\n74\t    checkpoint_after: true\n75\t  - name: \"Frozen, Not Deprecated\"\n76\t    objectives: [\"D2.1\"]\n77\t    requires_figure: false\n78\t    figure_anchor: null\n79\t    checkpoint_after: false\n80\t  - name: \"Roles, Not Just Routes\"\n81\t    objectives: [\"D2.1\"]\n82\t    requires_figure: true\n83\t    figure_anchor: \"ch10-fig03-gateway-api-role-split\"\n84\t    checkpoint_after: true\n85\t  - name: \"Allowing, Never Denying\"\n86\t    objectives: [\"D2.1\", \"D2.2\"]\n87\t    requires_figure: true\n88\t    figure_anchor: \"ch10-fig04-networkpolicy-additive-selectors\"\n89\t    checkpoint_after: false\n90\t  - name: \"What NetworkPolicy Cannot Do\"\n91\t    objectives: [\"D2.1\", \"D2.2\"]\n92\t    requires_figure: false\n93\t    figure_anchor: null\n94\t    checkpoint_after: true\n95\t  - name: \"Nothing Happens Without a Controller\"\n96\t    objectives: [\"D2.1\", \"D2.2\"]\n97\t    requires_figure: true\n98\t    figure_anchor: \"ch10-zenith-nothing-without-a-controller\"\n99\t    checkpoint_after: false\n100\t\n101\t#-- Eight sections against 5 weight points, matching Ch 9's count for two\n102\t#-- fewer points. The ratio is defensible because this chapter is TWO\n103\t#-- arcs, not one: an API-generations arc (§1–§5, Ingress → freeze →\n104\t#-- Gateway) and a policy arc (§6–§7), joined at §8 by a pattern that\n105\t#-- happens to be the failure mode of both. Fold options considered and\n106\t#-- rejected in § Open questions #10.\n107\t\n108\t#-- Skill v5.3 Part 11: Soundings pre-chapter diagnostic ------------------\n109\tsoundings_planned:\n110\t  question_count: 8\n111\t  topics:\n112\t    - \"one IP address serving several hostnames — the ordinary web-server prior, and what the server must read to tell them apart\"\n113\t    - \"retrieval from Ch 9 §3 — fifty services,